Business logic:

Payout exposure:

* exposure = amount * payoutMultiplier
* Default payoutMultiplier for 2D can be configurable, default to 400
* Do not hardcode this permanently; store it in draw or config

Tally update:
When a bet is accepted:

* Add amount to drawTallies/{drawId}/numbers/{number}.totalAmount
* Add exposure to drawTallies/{drawId}/numbers/{number}.exposure
* Increment betCount
* Recompute riskStatus

Risk status:

* riskPercent = exposure / riskLimit
* green if riskPercent < 0.60
* yellow if >= 0.60 and < 0.85
* orange if >= 0.85 and < 1.00
* red if >= 1.00
* blocked if manuallyBlocked = true

Submission behavior:

* If blocked, reject bet
* If red or over hard limit, create pendingApproval or reject depending config
* For MVP, make it pendingApproval so admin can decide
* Accepted and pendingApproval bets must be visible to admin
* Only accepted bets count toward active exposure
* If admin approves pendingApproval, then update tally
* If admin rejects, do not update tally

Security requirements:

* Use Firebase Auth
* Use Firestore Security Rules
* Agents can only read own user profile, open draws, risk flags needed for submission, and their own bets
* Agents can create bets only for themselves
* Agents cannot modify amount, number, drawId, agentId, branchId after creation
* Agents cannot read all bets
* Admins can read all bets, tallies, users, reports
* Admins can approve/reject/void according to permissions
* SuperAdmin can manage users, branches, and global config
* No public unauthenticated read/write
* Never trust client-only calculations for critical exposure; validate or recompute in transaction or Cloud Function where possible

